 /Event-Launch-Kit-CCS-20000-cEDH-Invitational-Qualifier-3.png
UID:liZgCenh0msW4GuLyvSW2
SUMMARY:CCS $20\,000 cEDH Invitational Qualifier #3
DTSTAMP:20260712T050313Z
DTSTART:20260801T090000Z
DESCRIPTION:🏆 CCS $20\,000 cEDH Invitational Qualifier #3 🏆\nThe race tight
	ens. The margins shrink. \nQualifier #3 brings us into the mid season of t
	he CCS $50\,000 cEDH Invitational Series. With only three events after\, e
	very decision matters and every point is gold. \nFull Details → https://to
	pdeck.gg/event/ccs-50000-cedh-invitational \n  \n🗓 Dates: August 1–2\, 202
	6 \n📍 Location: Charlie’s Collectible Show\, 9700 Bissonett St Unit 1500\,
	 Houston\, TX 77036 \n\nTournament Details:\n\n🎟️ Entry Fee: $90 before Jul
	y 18\, $110 After\n🔗 Register Now! 👉  https://topdeck.gg/event/css-20000-c
	edh-invitational-qualifier-4\n\n🗂️ Format & Structure\n\nFormat: cEDH (Prox
	y Friendly)\nSaturday: 6 Swiss Rounds (based on attendance)\nSunday: 2 Swi
	ss Rounds → Top 16\n\n🚫 Proxy Requirements: \n\nFull card name\, mana cost
	\, type line\, and effect text\nTest cards or clearly written MDFCs allowe
	d\nNo paper slip-ins permitted\n\n💰 Guaranteed $20\,000 Prize Pool\n\n1st 
	— $5\,000 + Auto Invite + TopDeck Invite + 200 pts\n2nd-4th — $2\,000 each
	 + Auto Invite + 160 pts\n5th–8th — $550 + 120 pts\n9th–16th — $550 + 100 
	pts\n17th–32nd — $175 + 75 pts\n33rd–48th — 60 pts\n49th–64th — 45 pts\n65
	th–96th — 30 pts\n97th–128th — 20 pts\n\nEvent Schedule:\n🕔 Registration O
	pens: 9 AM \n🕔 Player Meeting (Day 1): 10 AM \n🕔 Day 2 Start Time: 9 AM \n
	🛍️ Collectible Marketplace\nBetween rounds\, enjoy access to a curated mark
	etplace featuring: \n\nTCG singles\, sealed\, and accessories\nRetro video
	 games & consoles\nAnime merch\, figures\, and models\nToys and other hobb
	y collectibles\n\nPerfect for grabbing upgrades\, browsing grails\, or jus
	t hanging out between matches. \n🏨 Special Hotel Deals\nEnjoy a special ra
	te of $79/night — 2 Queens at TownePlace Suites\, only 15 minutes distance
	 from the action! \nBook your stay 👉🏻 https://www.marriott.com/event-reserv
	ations/reservation-link.mi?id=1767823967549&key=CORP&app=resvlink \n🔔 IMPO
	RTANT REMINDERS\n\nPlayer names will appear as real names on published doc
	uments.\nTop 16 decklists will be published.\n\n🔥 Late-season stakes hit h
	ard — tighten your game and push forward. Your run to the $50K Invitationa
	l continues at CCS cEDH Qualifier #3!\n\nhttps://ccs-houston.com/events/cc
	s-20000-cedh-invitational-qualifier-3/\n\nFrom CCS Houston
URL:https://ccs-houston.com/events/ccs-20000-cedh-invitational-qualifier-3/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ccs-houston
CATEGORIES:CCS Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT33H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ccs-houston.com/wp
 -content/uploads/2026/06/Banner.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ccs-houston.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 6/Banner.jpg
UID:wSC9XUmnL7Y_Rh4uPqk_W
SUMMARY:Houston Comic Exchange II
DTSTAMP:20260712T050313Z
DTSTART:20260801T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:Houston Comic Exchange II – Built for Comic Collectors\nSummer 
	is prime comic-hunting season\, and CCS Houston Comic Exchange II brings t
	ogether collectors\, dealers\, and fans for a day of buying\, selling\, tr
	ading\, and discovering comics. From key issues and first appearances to h
	idden gems and box-fresh finds\, every table offers something worth diggin
	g for. \nNo gatekeeping\, no pressure\, just comics and the people who lov
	e them. \n  \n📅 Saturday\, August 1\, 2026 | 10AM – 5PM \n📍 9700 Bissonnet
	 St\, Unit 1500\, Houston\, TX \n🎟️ FREE Entry + FREE Parking \n  \n🔥 Event
	 Highlights 🔥\n📦 50 Vendor Tables – All Comics\, All Formats \nSingles\, b
	ack issues\, key issues\, first appearances\, graded slabs\, raw runs\, in
	die and small press\, variant covers. Vendor tables dedicated entirely to 
	comics\, no toys\, no filler. If you’re a comic collector\, this floor was
	 built for you. \n  \n🔍 Key Issues and First Appearances \nThis is where t
	he hunt lives. Vendors bring the deep cuts\, raw back issues worth digging
	 through\, graded books if you’re chasing condition\, and the kind of keys
	 that actually show up when serious collectors are clearing their own coll
	ections to make room. \n  \n📚 Back-Issue Digging and Indie Discovery \nNot
	 every great find is a grail. Long boxes of back issues across decades and
	 publishers\, plus indie comics and small press titles that never make it 
	to a standard shop shelf. Come with a list or come ready to browse – both 
	work. \n  \n🤝 Vendors Who Collect Too \nThe people behind these tables are
	 the same people who will ask what you’re hunting before they start pullin
	g books for you. The Houston Comic Exchange is a community floor first. Th
	e conversations are part of the event. \n  \n🛒 Vendor Table Applications \
	nHouston comic vendors: we’re gathering a focused comics-only crowd\, and 
	free entry is driving serious foot traffic. Apply for your table here 👉🏻 ht
	tps://forms.gle/7q6pjcoiJTPbJouP8 \n  \nThe key issue you’ve been tracking
	 is probably in one of those long boxes this summer. The Houston Comic Exc
	hange II\, August 1. Free entry\, free parking\, always.\n\nhttps://ccs-ho
	uston.com/events/houston-comic-exchange-ii/\n\nFrom CCS Houston
URL:https://ccs-houston.com/events/houston-comic-exchange-ii/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ccs-houston
CATEGORIES:CCS Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT7H
END:VEVENT
